SELECTION / DEDUP / BOUNDS
One canonical NFC/lowercase (not casefold) token-sequence SHA256 groups sentence
variants. First uint64 big-endian mod10: 0=test, 1=dev, others=train. This is the
SAME split as round one, globally consistent across corpora/languages; existing
old test sentences found in a new source cannot become training. New source
sentences already present in the original corpus are excluded; selected new
sources deduplicate with each other, lexical-first source chooses display form.
All counts, vocabulary selection and display spelling use only train. No
cross-sentence lexical pairs, no context across invalid/number barriers.
The 30-candidate curve compares base-only/news/wiki/subtitles/all, K=3/6/12,
N=8000, min=10. Pick positive DE and EN mean dev recall@3 gains divided by combined
pack bytes, <=1MiB. Mean is equally weighted over original CV + new news/wiki/
subtitles validation domains (not token-pooled, not tested on final fixture).
Winner: all three new sources, K=3 in both languages. No corpus trigrams built:
there is no measured trigram gain to justify bytes; personal R2-2 trigrams stay.
Tradeoff accepted explicitly: larger encyclopedic/news coverage but full Tatoeba
heldout recall@3 drops DE 19.0541%->18.4022%, EN 28.1190%->27.5861%.
64-CV test improves DE 14.0625%->14.5089%, EN 17.7419%->18.4332%.
Packs 662793->770630 bytes (+107837); mapped+index payload 694793->802630.
Loader, format, N and combined 1MiB cap unchanged; no automatic-policy authority.

REPRODUCE (repository root; all external directories explicitly chosen)
1. Recreate original corpus.sqlite using README.md's build_d3b.py prepare $DATA.
   Original compile/verify reproduce ROUND ONE packs, intentionally unchanged.
   Keep those packs in $BASELINE, together with original heldout/reference JSON.
2. Download each URL above into its own newly created EMPTY directory under
   $DATA/raw-r2/<source>/; do not extract archives. Never execute contents. Match
   hashes in inputs.json. Adjust only path fields in a COPY of inputs.json to
   the explicit local download paths; keep SHA256/max_lines/source/kind unchanged.
3. Run:
python3 -I ios/tools/keyboard_context/tools/larger_corpora.py prepare /chosen/inputs.json /chosen/new.sqlite
python3 -I ios/tools/keyboard_context/tools/larger_corpora.py build /chosen/new.sqlite "$DATA/work-d3b/corpus.sqlite" "$BASELINE" /chosen/output
python3 -I ios/tools/keyboard_context/tools/evaluate_r2.py ios/tools/keyboard_context/tools/larger_corpora.py /chosen/new.sqlite "$DATA/work-d3b/corpus.sqlite" "$BASELINE" /chosen/output "$BASELINE/context-heldout-cc0.json" "$BASELINE/swift-reference-vectors.json"
python3 -I ios/tools/keyboard_context/tools/corpus_credits.py /chosen/de-wiki.tar.gz /chosen/wikipedia-de-sources.tsv.gz
python3 -I ios/tools/keyboard_context/tools/corpus_credits.py /chosen/en-wiki.tar.gz /chosen/wikipedia-en-sources.tsv.gz
python3 -I -m unittest discover -s ios/tools/keyboard_context -v
4. Independently repeat build to a new output directory; cmp both emitted packs.
   Install ONLY selected keyboard-{de,en}.tbg, generated reference vectors and
   context-heldout-r2.json into WordData; preserve the unchanged CC0 fixture.
   No raw corpora or SQLite files enter Git or app bundles. Per-download metadata,
   source-license evidence/failures and logs are retained externally under $DATA.
